   "source": [
    "# Clinical Frailty Scale (CFS) Calculator: Exploration and Guide\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook provides a guide to understanding, using, and modifying the Clinical Frailty Scale (CFS) calculator. The project has been refactored into a self-contained Python script (`cfs_calculator.py`) where the entire logic is defined in Python classes for maximum readability and maintainability."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Setup and Execution\n",
    "\n",
    "The main script reads patient data, calculates the CFS score for each patient, and saves the results. \n",
    "\n",
    "### Dependencies\n",
    "The script requires the following Python libraries:\n",
    "- `pandas`: For data manipulation.\n",
    "- `tqdm`: To display a progress bar.\n",
    "\n",
    "You can install them using pip:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install pandas tqdm"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Running the Calculator\n",
    "To run the full calculation process, execute the `cfs_calculator.py` script from your terminal. It will read the files from the `INPUT` directory and write the results to `OUTPUT/CFS_Results.csv`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# You would run this in your terminal\n",
    "# !python cfs_calculator.py"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. The CFS Algorithm Explained\n",
    "\n",
    "The core of the calculator is a decision tree, implemented in pure Python within the `CFSCalculator` class. This approach makes the logic explicit and easy to follow.\n",
    "\n",
    "The tree is constructed in the `_build_decision_tree` method. Here is the exact logic that determines a patient's score:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def _build_decision_tree(self) -> DecisionNode:\n",
    "    ""Builds the CFS decision tree using DecisionNode and ResultNode objects."""\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Leaf nodes (results)\n",
    "    cfs_1 = ResultNode(1, \"Very Fit\")\n",
    "    cfs_2 = ResultNode(2, \"Fit\")\n",
    "    cfs_3 = ResultNode(3, \"Managing Well\")\n",
    "    cfs_4 = ResultNode(4, \"Living with Very Mild Frailty\")\n",
    "    cfs_5 = ResultNode(5, \"Living with Mild Frailty\")\n",
    "    cfs_6 = ResultNode(6, \"Living with Moderate Frailty\")\n",
    "    cfs_7 = ResultNode(7, \"Living with Severe Frailty\")\n",
    "    cfs_8 = ResultNode(8, \"Living with Very Severe Frailty, Totally Dependent\")\n",
    "    cfs_9 = ResultNode(9, \"Terminally Ill\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Decision branches, built from the bottom up for clarity\n",
    "    \n",
    "    engages_activity_no_for_fit = DecisionNode(\"engages_in_strenuous_activity\", \"equal\", False, cfs_2, cfs_1)\n",
    "    fit_or_very_fit_branch = DecisionNode(\"effort_to_perform_tasks\", \"equal\", \"rarely_never\", engages_activity_no_for_fit, cfs_4) # Simplified this branch\n",
    "\n",
    "    engages_activity_no_for_managing = DecisionNode(\"engages_in_strenuous_activity\", \"equal\", False, cfs_3, cfs_2)\n",
    "    managing_well_branch = DecisionNode(\"effort_to_perform_tasks\", \"equal\", \"sometimes_occasionally\", engages_activity_no_for_managing, fit_or_very_fit_branch)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    health_branch = DecisionNode(\"self_rated_health\", \"in\", [\"Fair\", \"Poor\"], cfs_4, managing_well_branch)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    chronic_condition_branch = DecisionNode(\"chronic_condition_count\", \"greater_than_or_equal\", 10, cfs_4, health_branch)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    iadl_range_branch = DecisionNode(\"iadl_count\", \"in_range\", [1, 4], cfs_5, cfs_6)\n",
    "    iadl_branch = DecisionNode(\"iadl_count\", \"greater_than_or_equal\", 1, iadl_range_branch, chronic_condition_branch)\n",
    "\n",
    "    badl_1_2_branch = DecisionNode(\"badl_count\", \"in_range\", [1, 2], cfs_6, iadl_branch)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    badl_3_5_branch = DecisionNode(\"badl_count\", \"in_range\", [3, 5], cfs_8, cfs_7) # if not 3-5, must be > 5\n",
    "    badl_branch = DecisionNode(\"badl_count\", \"greater_than_or_equal\", 3, badl_3_5_branch, badl_1_2_branch)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    root = DecisionNode(\"is_terminally_ill\", \"equal\", True, cfs_9, badl_branch)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return root"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### How to Tweak the Algorithm\n",
    "\n",
    "Since the logic is pure Python, tweaking it is straightforward.\n",
    "\n",
    "1.  **Open `cfs_calculator.py`** in a code editor.\n",
    "2.  **Navigate to the `_build_decision_tree` method** inside the `CFSCalculator` class.\n",
    "3.  **Modify the logic directly.** You can change thresholds, re-wire branches, or add new `DecisionNode`s.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example:** Let's say you want to change the threshold for \"Vulnerable\" (CFS 4) from 10 chronic conditions to 8.\n",
    "\n",
    "You would change this line:\n",
    "```python\n",
    "# OLD\n",
    "chronic_condition_branch = DecisionNode(\"chronic_condition_count\", \"greater_than_or_equal\", 10, cfs_4, health_branch)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "To this:\n",
    "```python\n",
    "# NEW\n",
    "chronic_condition_branch = DecisionNode(\"chronic_condition_count\", \"greater_than_or_equal\", 8, cfs_4, health_branch)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "After saving the file, re-running `cfs_calculator.py` will use your new logic."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's load the results and perform some basic analysis."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import plotly.express as px\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    results_df = pd.read_csv('OUTPUT/CFS_Results.csv')\n",
    "    print(\"Results loaded successfully.\")\n",
    "    display(results_df.head())\n",
    "except FileNotFoundError:\n",
    "    print(\"Results file not found. Please run the main script first.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Distribution of CFS Scores\n",
    "A bar chart is a good way to see how many patients fall into each frailty category."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if 'results_df' in locals():\n",
    "    cfs_counts = results_df['cfs_score'].value_counts().sort_index()\n",
    "\n",
    "    fig = px.bar(\n",
    "        x=cfs_counts.index, \n",
    "        y=cfs_counts.values,\n",
    "        labels={'x': 'CFS Score', 'y': 'Number of Patients'},
    "        title='Distribution of Clinical Frailty Scale (CFS) Scores',\n",
    "        text=cfs_counts.values\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    fig.update_traces(textposition='outside')\n",
    "    fig.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. How to Run Tests\n",
    "\n",
    "When you modify the algorithm, it's crucial to test your changes to prevent unexpected results. Because the logic is encapsulated in a class, it's easy to unit test.\n",
    "\n",
    "We recommend creating a separate test file, for example `test_cfs_calculator.py`, and using Python's built-in `unittest` framework.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Example Test File\n",
    "Here is an example of what `test_cfs_calculator.py` could look like. It tests two specific scenarios."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import unittest\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from cfs_calculator import CFSCalculator\n",
    "\n",
    "class TestCFSCalculator(unittest.TestCase):\n",
    "\n",
    "    def setUp(self):\n",
    "        """Set up the calculator for all tests."""\n",
    "        self.calculator = CFSCalculator()\n",
    "\n",
    "    def test_cfs_9_terminally_ill(self):\n",
    "        """Test that a terminally ill patient correctly scores CFS 9."""\n",
    "        # Create sample data for a patient who is terminally ill\n",
    "        patient_data = pd.Series({'PatientNum': 1})\n",
    "        diagnosis_data = pd.DataFrame([\n",
    "            {'PatientNum': 1, 'Name': 'some other illness'},\n",
    "            {'PatientNum': 1, 'Name': 'end-stage renal disease'}\n",
    "        ])\n",
    "\n",
    "        result = self.calculator.calculate(patient_data, diagnosis_data)\n",
    "        self.assertEqual(result['cfs_score'], 9)\n",
    "        print(f"\\nTest 'test_cfs_9_terminally_ill' passed: Score={result['cfs_score']}")\n",
    "\n",
    "    def test_cfs_1_very_fit(self):\n",
    "        """Test that a very fit patient correctly scores CFS 1."""\n",
    "        # Create sample data for a patient with no issues\n",
    "        patient_data = pd.Series({\n",
    "            'PatientNum': 2,\n",
    "            'מצב תפקודי': 'עצמאי',\n",
    "            'מצב פיזי': 'טוב'\n",
    "            # Add other data points to simulate 'rarely_never' effort and 'engages_in_strenuous_activity' = True\n",
    "            # For a complete test, one would need to mock the fact generation\n",
    "        })\n",
    "        diagnosis_data = pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # For this example, we will manually create the facts that the tree needs\n",
    "        patient_facts = {\n",
    "            'is_terminally_ill': False,\n",
    "            'badl_count': 0,\n",
    "            'iadl_count': 0,\n",
    "            'chronic_condition_count': 1,\n",
    "            'self_rated_health': 'Very Good/Good',\n",
    "            'effort_to_perform_tasks': 'rarely_never',\n",
    "            'engages_in_strenuous_activity': True\n",
    "        }\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # We can test the tree evaluation directly\n",
    "        result_node = self.calculator.decision_tree.evaluate(patient_facts)\n",
    "        self.assertEqual(result_node.score, 1)\n",
    "        print(f"Test 'test_cfs_1_very_fit' passed: Score={result_node.score}")\n",
    "\n",
    "# To run the tests from your terminal:\n",
    "# !python -m unittest test_cfs_calculator.py\n",
    "\n",
    "# To run in a notebook, you can use the following:\n",
    "if __name__ == '__main__':\n",
    "    suite = unittest.TestSuite()\n",
    "    suite.addTest(unittest.makeSuite(TestCFSCalculator))\n",
    "    runner = unittest.TextTestRunner()\n",
    "    runner.run(suite)"
   ]
  }
